# Expectation record for 02_constant_expressions/001_arithmetic_constant_folding.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 001_arithmetic_constant_folding
area               = 02_constant_expressions
description        = Constant arithmetic folded at compile time, each property paired line-for-line with a volatile-operand runtime twin the backend must compute instead of reading the folder's answer
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined behaviour and depends on no unspecified behaviour, which is the
precondition that makes both differential oracles sound rather than a stylistic preference:
undefined behaviour would license either compiler to do anything at all, so a divergence between
them would prove nothing about either one. The paragraphs below are the written argument required of
every program in this suite; the warning gate and the sanitizer gate are its machine half.
NO ARITHMETIC CAN OVERFLOW. Every operand is a small literal or a volatile object initialized from
one, and every folded value and its runtime twin are the small numbers printed in the golden below.
The widest int value the program forms anywhere -- operand, intermediate or printed result -- is
4095, and the largest magnitude any negative int reaches is 1024, so every int computation here sits
inside the MINIMUM range C11 5.2.4.2.1 guarantees for the type, -32767 to 32767, let alone the 32-bit
range all four enabled targets actually provide. The wide arithmetic is performed in long long
throughout, built from LL-suffixed literals: the largest product is
100000 * 100000 == 10000000000, the largest sum is 1234567890123 + 876543210987 == 2111111101110, and
the largest shift result is 1LL << 40 == 1099511627776. The standard fixes long long at a minimum of
64 bits, so all three are orders of magnitude inside its range on every enabled target -- including
the 32-bit one -- and neither the folded nor the runtime form can overflow. Plain long is never used,
which also removes the width difference recorded under implementation-defined notes. The negation,
subtraction and unary-minus lines are applied to operands whose magnitude is far from the minimum of
their type, so no negation is undefined, and no signed addition, subtraction or multiplication
approaches INT_MAX, INT_MIN or the long long limits, so the one genuinely undefined arithmetic case
in C cannot arise.
NO DIVISION IS UNDEFINED. Every divisor is a non-zero literal, or a volatile object initialized from
a non-zero literal and never modified afterwards. The complete set of them is 7 in the division and
remainder lines, 3 in the two precedence lines, 4 and then 2 in the left-associative division line,
1 in the division-identity line, and 7LL in the two wide lines, so no divisor anywhere can be zero.
The one remaining undefined division, the most negative value divided by -1, is never formed: no
division or remainder in this file has INT_MIN or LLONG_MIN as its left operand, and no divisor is
negative. The remainder operator's operands are the same values as the division's. Every dividend is
positive as well, so neither the direction of truncation nor the sign of a remainder even arises as a
question here -- and C11 6.5.5p6 fixes both in any case, as truncation toward zero and a remainder
taking the dividend's sign, both of which were measured identical on all four targets.
EVERY SHIFT IS IN RANGE. Each shift count is a non-negative constant, or a volatile object
initialized from one in its own declaration and never modified: 10, 3 and 4 against 32-bit int left
operands, and 40 against a 64-bit long long left operand, each strictly below the width of its
promoted left operand. Only non-negative values are left-shifted, which forecloses the undefined
signed left-shift case and means no left shift discards a sign bit. Exactly one negative value
appears in a shift, -1024, and it appears only as the left operand of a RIGHT shift, which C11
6.5.7p5 makes implementation-defined rather than undefined; the impl_defined_notes below account for
it.
NO STORAGE IS READ UNINITIALIZED and no object is modified twice between sequence points. Every
object in the program is initialized in its own declaration and none is assigned to afterwards, so
there is no second modification anywhere to sequence against a first, and no expression modifies an
object whose prior value is read for a purpose other than computing the value to be stored.
NO EVALUATION ORDER IS DEPENDED UPON, and the argument for that deliberately does not rest on
counting the volatile reads, because several lines do read one object twice: v1337 - v1337 is the
sharpest, and v3 and v9 each appear twice in a precedence line and again in the mixed-logic line. It
rests on something stronger. No volatile object is ever WRITTEN, so every read of one yields the
value its own declaration gave it, and therefore neither the number of accesses -- which C11 6.7.3p7
leaves implementation-defined, so a record may not assume it -- nor the order they happen in can
change a printed byte. Each printf call takes its format string and exactly one value argument, so
there is no second argument whose evaluation could interleave with it, and the two short-circuit
lines impose their own sequencing on their operands rather than relying on an unspecified order.
THE ONLY POINTERS IN THIS PROGRAM ARE THE FORMAT STRINGS. No object address is taken, no array of
the program's own is declared and no aggregate is declared, so the only pointer values that exist
are the ones the string literals decay to at each printf call -- never printed, never compared,
never converted to an integer and never arithmetic operands. There is therefore no aliasing rule to
break, no one-past-the-end question to answer, no object representation to inspect, no padding byte
to observe and no dependence on the relative addresses of unrelated objects.
OUTPUT IS FULLY DETERMINISTIC: no address, no timestamp, no randomness, no locale-dependent
formatting, literal loop bounds throughout, and main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite
requires so that no exit status is truncated by the operating system. Every input is a literal in
this file, so every cell is reproducible from this source and this record alone.
NO HEADER IS NAMED ANYWHERE and the single libc prototype the program needs, printf, is declared by
hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`. bcc bundles the nine required freestanding headers plus a
bonus stdatomic.h and ships no standard I/O header (docs/project-guide.md line 212), so a directive
naming that header would fail on the bcc side of oracle (a) while succeeding on the reference side --
a spurious divergence caused by the test rather than by the compiler under test. Nothing in the file
is a GCC extension, so no include exception and no gate deviation is available to area 02 and none is
needed; the corpus has exactly two header exceptions, area 07's stdarg.h and the dedicated
bundled-header probe in area 12.
THIS RECORD DECLARES NO WARNING-GATE DEVIATION: no ub_audit_flags key appears above, so the program
is audited under the suite's full default gate. It is clean under -Wall -Wextra -pedantic
-Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror in the single native compile-only invocation the
suite's warning gate makes, and it builds and runs clean under the sanitizer gate
-fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all. Both gates are reference-compiler-only and
are never applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is untouched.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This record narrows nothing. All four targets, all three optimization levels and all three
oracles are enabled, and no expected-divergence marker is attached. These notes exist to
record how that was achieved, because a program in this area could easily have had to narrow:
constant evaluation reaches straight into the type system, which is where the four
supported targets differ.
THE TWO-VARIANT RULE AND WHY BOTH HALVES ARE NEEDED. Every property is printed twice: once
from a constant expression, so the answer comes from the constant evaluator, and once from
volatile-qualified operands, which no implementation may read at translation time, so that
answer comes from the code generator. Every fold_ line is printed immediately above the runtime_
line that recomputes the same value, and their equality is the two-variant assertion this program
exists to make. The mechanism rests on the language rather than on any compiler's habits: an access
to a volatile object is an observable side effect, so no implementation may satisfy the runtime half
by folding the value at translation time -- it must store the object, load it back and do the
arithmetic, whatever instructions it chooses for the arithmetic itself -- where the non-volatile form
may collapse to a single immediate. Without the runtime half, optimization substitutes
the folder's answer for the backend's and a code-generation defect escapes detection entirely
while the suite still reports a pass. With it, a divergent fold_ line accuses the constant
evaluator, a divergent runtime_ line accuses the backend, and a pair that disagrees with itself
accuses one of the two.
WIDTH NORMALIZATION. sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) were MEASURED at 4 bytes on i686 and 8
bytes on x86-64, AArch64 and RISC-V 64 (docs/technical-specifications.md target table, lines
457-462), so no plain long, no size_t, no ptrdiff_t and no pointer value is printed anywhere.
Where the program computes a value too wide for int, that value is written in long long with
LL-suffixed literals and printed with %lld, which is 64 bits on every enabled target; every
other value reaches stdout through %d, and every one of those arguments already HAS type int.
That is checked rather than arranged by casting: the program declares no unsigned type and
contains no cast anywhere at all, so there is no conversion left for a width difference to act
on. Those two conversions are the entire format vocabulary of the program, no sizeof result is
printed, and no floating value reaches a format string, so no width that differs between the
ILP32 backend and the three LP64 backends can influence a byte of stdout.
PLAIN-char SIGNEDNESS. Plain char was MEASURED as signed on x86-64 and i686 and unsigned on
AArch64 and RISC-V 64. No plain-char value is printed and no printed line depends on that
choice, so a divergence that is not a compiler defect cannot arise from it here.
RIGHT SHIFT OF A NEGATIVE VALUE IS THE FIRST OF THE TWO IMPLEMENTATION-DEFINED PROPERTIES THIS
PROGRAM OBSERVES -- the second is the signed integer representation, recorded further down -- AND
IT IS OBSERVED DELIBERATELY. C11 6.5.7p5 leaves the result of E1 >> E2 implementation-defined
when E1 has a signed type and a negative value, so fold_shr_negative and
runtime_shr_negative print a value the standard does not fix. All four supported targets
were MEASURED to perform an ARITHMETIC (sign-propagating) shift with the four reference drivers
oracle (a) uses, so both lines read -64 on every cell of the matrix rather than a large positive
value, and the property is therefore safe for cross-backend comparison as it stands. It is kept
in the comparison rather than removed because a right shift of a negative value is exactly where
a backend's choice between an arithmetic and a logical shift instruction becomes observable, and
that choice is a code-generation decision this suite exists to check. A left shift of a negative
value, which would be undefined rather than implementation-defined, is never formed anywhere in
the program.
WHAT WOULD LEGITIMATELY BREAK EITHER OF THOSE, AND HOW IT MUST THEN BE HANDLED. A conforming
target on which the right shift of a negative value were logical, on which a signed integer were
not two's complement, or on which int or long long had a different width, would produce a
different value here without being defective. That would be an implementation-defined divergence
rather than a compiler defect, and the correct response would be to narrow this record's target
list and record the reason in this field -- never to charge a defect against a backend that did
nothing wrong, and never to delete the shift, the complement or the wide arithmetic, which
requirement 2 asks this program to cover and whose removal would remove coverage of the two
integer operators whose signed behaviour the standard declines to fix.
SIGNED DIVISION AND REMAINDER NEED NO ACCOUNTING. C99 onwards fixes integer division as
truncation toward zero and the remainder as taking the dividend's sign (C11 6.5.5p6), so
fold_div, fold_mod, fold_ll_div, fold_ll_mod and their twins are determined by the standard
rather than by the implementation, fixing fold_div=14, fold_mod=2, fold_ll_div=1428571428 and
fold_ll_mod=4. Both properties were nonetheless MEASURED identical on all four targets before
this record was written.
SIGNED INTEGER REPRESENTATION IS THE SECOND IMPLEMENTATION-DEFINED PROPERTY THIS PROGRAM
OBSERVES, THROUGH THE ONE OPERATOR THAT MAKES IT VISIBLE. C11 6.2.6.2p2 permits a signed integer
to be two's complement, ones' complement or sign-and-magnitude and leaves the choice to the
implementation, and C11 6.5.3.3p4 defines ~ as the complement of every bit of the converted
operand -- so the value of ~1023 follows from that choice, and fold_complement and
runtime_complement print it. Two's complement gives -1024, which is what all four targets were
MEASURED to print; ones' complement would give -1023 and sign-and-magnitude a large negative
value, so this is a real dependence rather than a formality, and it is stated here rather than
waved away. It is kept in the comparison for the same reason the shift is: the complement of a
signed value is a printed value the constant evaluator and the code generator have to agree on
bit for bit, which is the agreement this program exists to check -- and the runtime twin really
does reach the backend, because its operand is volatile and so may not be folded. Every target this
suite supports is two's complement, and C23 6.2.6.2 has since made that the only permitted
representation, so the dependence is safe on all four backends and cross-backend comparison of
these two lines is sound as it stands. Nothing else in the program touches the representation:
no value is produced by overflow, no object representation is inspected byte by byte, and no
negative value is reinterpreted through another type.
EXECUTION CHARACTER SET: NOT ENGAGED, VERIFIED RATHER THAN ASSERTED. C11 5.2.1 leaves the
members of the execution character set and their codes implementation-defined, so a program
that printed a character's numeric code, or rendered a literal as bytes, would owe an
accounting here. This one owes none: it contains no character constant at all -- checked
mechanically, by stripping comments and string literals and finding zero -- and derives no
printed VALUE from a character. Its only string literals are the printf format strings, and it
declares no _Static_assert message either, so the whole of its literal text is fixed label text
that is byte-identical in all twelve cells of the matrix and in the golden below. There is
therefore no code to pin and nothing to narrow. That is precisely what distinguishes this program
from 004_sizeof_alignof.c and 007_string_literal_constants.c in the same area, both of
which do print character codes and both of which pin every code they print with a
_Static_assert for that reason.
HERMETIC AND DETERMINISTIC. Every input is a literal in the source: nothing is read from the
clock, the environment, the command line, a file or a socket, and nothing is written anywhere.
Output is one line per semantic property claimed, in a fixed order, so a single divergent line
names the construct that produced it. No address or pointer value is printed, there is no
randomness, no locale-dependent formatting and no data-dependent iteration order, and the program
returns 0 -- well inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is
truncated by the operating system.
MEASURED EVIDENCE. The program was compiled with the reference driver for all four targets at
-O0, -O1 and -O2 -- twelve configurations -- and every one produced these 82 lines
byte-identically with exit status 0, which is why cross-backend comparison is sound, oracle (b)
is enabled with no narrowing, and oracle (c) can hold these bytes as the golden record.
END
